    [Doc][Misc] Align all EPLB documentation with the code (#19377)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    > Companion of #19369 (the `releases/v0.30.0` backport). The two PRs are
    identical except for one row: W4A8 MXFP is **rejected** here because
    main does not include #18444 (`supports_eplb = False` in
    `w4a8_mxfp4.py`), while v0.30 enabled it.
    
    A full pass over every EPLB-related page on `main`, cross-checked
    field-by-field against the implementation (`ascend_config.py`,
    `platform.py`, `patch/platform/patch_eplb.py`, `worker/v2/eplb.py`,
    `distributed/eplb/**`, `eplb/**`, `model_runner_v1.py`, quantization
    `supports_eplb` declarations, and upstream vLLM `EPLBConfig`). Every
    documented default, range, error message, log string, and example was
    verified against code; an independent documentation-review pass then
    re-verified all findings before this PR.
    
    Main fixes:
    
    **User guide (`expert_parallelism_load_balancer.md`)**
    - Weight-format matrix: W4A16 / W4A16 MXFP / W4A8 MXFP rejection is
    clarified as layout-based (`supports_eplb = False`) on all hardware, not
    950-specific.
    - The MRv2 quick start contradicted its own "STAIR defaults do not
    require tuning" advice (window_size 50 / step_interval 50 / redundant
    defaults). It is now split into a minimal production command and a
    short-run validation command (window_size/step_interval 200) with an
    explicit warning.
    - `log_balancedness` is documented as recommended-off: it is off by
    default, incurs extra communication, and neither it nor
    `log_balancedness_interval` appears in the recommended example
    configuration (only as a temporary debugging step in the monitoring
    section).
    - New **Advanced STAIR Tuning** section documenting all `stair_config`
    fields, defaults, and validated ranges — this section was referenced by
    `additional_config.md#advanced-stair-tuning` but did not exist (dead
    anchor).
    - `load_collection_phase`: documented that it only takes effect with the
    STAIR policy (the phase filter is gated on `uses_custom_load_stats` in
    `worker/v2/eplb.py`), that values other than `all` require
    `--enable-eplb`, that non-matching batches still advance the shared
    window, and that a fully non-matching phase skips the next rearrangement
    instead of running on an empty window.
    - Monitoring: corrected the MRv1 log anchor from the nonexistent
    `[Expert Hotness]` to the real `[eplb/worker] Expert hotness imbalance`
    line and added MRv2 log anchors; precise env-var accepted values
    (`DYNAMIC_EPLB` case-insensitive `true`/`1`, `EXPERT_MAP_RECORD` exactly
    lowercase `true`).
    - Removed the stale "Static EPLB scheduled for removal in v0.25.1"
    warning; described the Random policy accurately (fixed expert pair,
    needs >= 4 EP ranks); recommend absolute paths for
    `expert_map_record_path`; added the MRv1 update-cycle formula and
    communicator-selection log-level correction (clamp logs info, preserved
    explicit values log warning).
    
    **`additional_config.md`**: fixed "asynchronous Gloo movement" to
    HIXL-by-default with Gloo fallback, added the `stair_config` row, and
    stated the `load_collection_phase` constraints.
    
    **Design docs**: `model_runner_v1_eplb.md` — removed the nonexistent
    `eplb/utils.py` from the module tree, replaced the stale DFX code
    samples with the actual `EplbConfig` validation behavior, aligned the
    `rebalance_experts` contract (`(changed_flag, per_layer_priority,
    new_expert_table)`) and the new-MoE-model integration steps with the
    current adaptor, and documented the runtime lifecycle (subprocess,
    iteration formula, heat classification). `model_runner_v2_eplb.md` —
    STAIR is the default policy, phase filtering only applies to
    custom-load-stats policies, initial redundant experts are spread
    round-robin (differs from upstream), corrected the committed-cycle log
    semantics (imbalance ratios, lower is better), and added debug log
    anchors.
    
    **Support matrix**: Expert Parallel row now says STAIR is the default
    Ascend policy (was "upstream default policy"); the feature-matrix EPLB
    link points to the user guide instead of the v1-only design doc.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation-only. No code, config, or behavior changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Every technical claim was verified against main's EPLB code and
    upstream vLLM sources (field defaults, validation error strings, log
    formats, supported-format matrix, test file names). The single
    branch-specific divergence (W4A8 MXFP) was identified and handled
    explicitly.
    - An independent documentation-review agent re-verified all claims
    against the v0.30 code base (identical EPLB code except #18444), found 1
    major + 4 minor + 3 nit issues, all fixed and re-verified to ACCEPT in a
    second round.
    - `bash format.sh ci` passes (markdownlint included).
    - CI verification is sufficient for a documentation-only change.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
